## 8) Minimal SMARTS pattern library (starter set)
Use these with `match_substructure` to drive boosts/penalties (extend as needed):

```python
patterns = {
  # Covalent/latent electrophiles (context matters)
  "nitrile": "C#N",
  "terminal_alkyne": "[CH]#C",
  "alkyne_any": "C#C",
  "aldehyde": "[CH](=O)",
  "alpha_ketoamide": "C(=O)C(=O)N",
  "michael_acceptor_enone": "C=CC(=O)",
  "acrylamide": "C=CC(=O)N",
  "vinyl_sulfone": "S(=O)(=O)C=CC",
  "chloroacetamide": "ClCC(=O)N",
  "epoxide": "C1OC1",

  # Protease-inhibitor shape cues
  "lactam_2_pyrrolidone": "O=C1NCCC1",
  "amide": "C(=O)N",
  "trifluoromethyl": "C(F)(F)F",

  # TMPRSS2-like S1 binders
  "amidine": "C(=N)N",
  "guanidine": "NC(=N)N",
  "benzamidine_like": "c1ccccc1C(=N)N",

  # PAINS-ish / redox / thiol-reactive flags
  "catechol": "c1ccc(O)c(O)c1",
  "quinone": "O=c1ccc(=O)cc1",
  "disulfide": "SS",
  "selenium": "[Se]",
}
```

